@lang en

-- tests-time.l4 : tests for us-interpretation-time.l4
-- Expected values come from the text of Title 1, never from the code. Title 1 has no rule on any of the six items,
-- so every expected answer in Part A is a refusal, pinned to its own message with BECAUSE.
-- Part B expectations are the ordinary reading of the words of ss 106, 204 and 112b/202(c); the dates are worked
-- by hand from the calendar and written down here before the run.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `us-interpretation-time`

§ `Fixtures`

`one day`    MEANS `A period` WITH `how many` IS 1,  `counted in` IS days
`one week`   MEANS `A period` WITH `how many` IS 1,  `counted in` IS weeks
`one month`  MEANS `A period` WITH `how many` IS 1,  `counted in` IS months
`one year`   MEANS `A period` WITH `how many` IS 1,  `counted in` IS years
`thirty days` MEANS `A period` WITH `how many` IS 30, `counted in` IS days
`two years`  MEANS `A period` WITH `how many` IS 2,  `counted in` IS years
`three years` MEANS `A period` WITH `how many` IS 3, `counted in` IS years
`four years` MEANS `A period` WITH `how many` IS 4,  `counted in` IS years
`five years` MEANS `A period` WITH `how many` IS 5,  `counted in` IS years

-- 2026-02-14 is a Saturday, 2026-02-15 a Sunday, 2026-02-16 a Monday. The list is an INPUT supplied here;
-- nothing in the module knows any of these dates is a day of rest.
`a day of rest and the day after it` MEANS LIST (YMD 2026 2 14), (YMD 2026 2 15)
`three days in a row` MEANS LIST (YMD 2026 2 14), (YMD 2026 2 15), (YMD 2026 2 16)

§ `Item 1 — a period of days or weeks counted from a day`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of days or weeks counted from a day` `thirty days` (YMD 2026 1 1) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of days from a day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of days or weeks counted from a day` `one day` (YMD 2026 1 1) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of days from a day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of days or weeks counted from a day` `one week` (YMD 2026 1 1) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of weeks from a day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of days or weeks counted from a day` `thirty days` (YMD 2026 1 1) `a day of rest and the day after it` BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of days from a day"
-- a start on the 31st and on 29 February, in days
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of days or weeks counted from a day` `thirty days` (YMD 2026 1 31) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of days from a day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of days or weeks counted from a day` `thirty days` (YMD 2024 2 29) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of days from a day"
-- the function is given a month: the answer is still that Title 1 has no rule
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of days or weeks counted from a day` `one month` (YMD 2026 1 1) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of months after an event"

§ `Item 2 — a period of months or years counted after an event`

-- the brief's worked cases
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of months or years counted after an event` `three years` (YMD 2025 7 16) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of years after an event"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of months or years counted after an event` `five years` (YMD 2025 1 15) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of years after an event"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of months or years counted after an event` `five years` (YMD 2025 9 1) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of years after an event"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of months or years counted after an event` `two years` (YMD 2024 2 28) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of years after an event"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of months or years counted after an event` `one year` (YMD 2024 2 29) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of years after an event"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of months or years counted after an event` `one month` (YMD 2025 1 31) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of months after an event"
-- one year, one month, other starts: a leap day four years on, a 30-day month, a start in December
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of months or years counted after an event` `four years` (YMD 2024 2 29) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of years after an event"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of months or years counted after an event` `one month` (YMD 2026 3 31) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of months after an event"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of months or years counted after an event` `one month` (YMD 2026 12 31) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of months after an event"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of months or years counted after an event` `one year` (YMD 2025 1 15) `a day of rest and the day after it` BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of years after an event"
-- the function is given days: the answer is still that Title 1 has no rule
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of months or years counted after an event` `one week` (YMD 2026 1 1) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for counting a period of weeks from a day"

§ `Item 3 — a last day that is a day of rest, recess or holiday`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period once days of rest, recess or holiday are allowed for` `thirty days` (YMD 2026 2 14) `a day of rest and the day after it` BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for a last day that is a day of rest, recess or holiday"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period once days of rest, recess or holiday are allowed for` `thirty days` (YMD 2026 2 15) `a day of rest and the day after it` BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for a last day that is a day of rest, recess or holiday"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period once days of rest, recess or holiday are allowed for` `thirty days` (YMD 2026 2 14) `three days in a row` BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for a last day that is a day of rest, recess or holiday"
-- a last day that is NOT on the list: Title 1 still has no rule, and the answer is still a refusal, never the day itself
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period once days of rest, recess or holiday are allowed for` `thirty days` (YMD 2026 2 13) `a day of rest and the day after it` BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for a last day that is a day of rest, recess or holiday"
-- months and years, and an empty list
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period once days of rest, recess or holiday are allowed for` `one month` (YMD 2026 2 14) `a day of rest and the day after it` BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for a last day that is a day of rest, recess or holiday"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period once days of rest, recess or holiday are allowed for` `one year` (YMD 2026 2 14) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule for a last day that is a day of rest, recess or holiday"

§ `Item 4 — whether a date falls inside a period`

-- counted from a day: the last day inside and the next day outside cannot be located, so each is a refusal
#ASSERT REFUSED `a date falls inside a period counted from a day or after an event` (YMD 2026 1 31) `thirty days` (YMD 2026 1 1) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no counting rule, so it cannot say whether a date falls inside a period"
#ASSERT REFUSED `a date falls inside a period counted from a day or after an event` (YMD 2026 1 30) `thirty days` (YMD 2026 1 1) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no counting rule, so it cannot say whether a date falls inside a period"
#ASSERT REFUSED `a date falls inside a period counted from a day or after an event` (YMD 2026 2 1) `thirty days` (YMD 2026 1 1) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no counting rule, so it cannot say whether a date falls inside a period"
#ASSERT REFUSED `a date falls inside a period counted from a day or after an event` (YMD 2025 1 15) `one year` (YMD 2024 1 15) EMPTY BECAUSE "Title 1 has no counting rule, so it cannot say whether a date falls inside a period"

-- the arithmetic that is not a rule: a date lies on or between two days the caller already holds
#ASSERT NOT `a date lies on or between the first day given and the last day given` (YMD 2026 1 14) (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 20)
#ASSERT     `a date lies on or between the first day given and the last day given` (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 20)
#ASSERT     `a date lies on or between the first day given and the last day given` (YMD 2026 1 17) (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 20)
#ASSERT     `a date lies on or between the first day given and the last day given` (YMD 2026 1 20) (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 20)
#ASSERT NOT `a date lies on or between the first day given and the last day given` (YMD 2026 1 21) (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 20)
#ASSERT     `a date lies on or between the first day given and the last day given` (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `a date lies on or between the first day given and the last day given` (YMD 2026 1 16) (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 15)

§ `Item 5 — the day, and the moment within the day, from which an Act binds`

-- Case: an Act is passed or published on 2026-03-10 and says nothing about when it comes into force
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day from which an Act binds` `it says nothing about when it comes into force` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "Title 1 does not say from what day an Act binds when the Act does not say"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the moment within its commencement day from which an Act binds` `it says nothing about when it comes into force` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "Title 1 does not say from what moment of its commencement day an Act binds"
-- Case: an Act says it comes into force on a day to be fixed later; the day is fixed as 2026-06-01
#ASSERT `the day from which an Act binds` (`it fixes a day` (YMD 2026 6 1)) (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
#ASSERT REFUSED `the moment within its commencement day from which an Act binds` (`it fixes a day` (YMD 2026 6 1)) (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "Title 1 does not say from what moment of its commencement day an Act binds"
-- the day fixed is the Act's own word even when it falls before the day the Act is passed: Title 1 does not say otherwise
#ASSERT `the day from which an Act binds` (`it fixes a day` (YMD 2026 3 1)) (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1

§ `Item 6 — the day subordinate legislation comes into force`

-- Case: subordinate legislation is made on 2026-03-10 and says nothing about when it comes into force
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day from which subordinate legislation comes into force` `it says nothing about when it comes into force` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "Title 1 does not say when subordinate legislation comes into force when it does not say"
-- where the instrument fixes a day, that day is its own word
#ASSERT `the day from which subordinate legislation comes into force` (`it fixes a day` (YMD 2026 4 1)) (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 1

§ `Deemed service or notice, and the meanings of the time words`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the day a document is treated as served` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "Title 1 has no rule on when a document is treated as served or a notice as given"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the meaning Title 1 gives to a time word` `the word day` BECAUSE "Title 1 gives no meaning to the word day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the meaning Title 1 gives to a time word` `the word week` BECAUSE "Title 1 gives no meaning to the word week"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the meaning Title 1 gives to a time word` `the word month` BECAUSE "Title 1 gives no meaning to the word month"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the meaning Title 1 gives to a time word` `the word year` BECAUSE "Title 1 gives no meaning to the word year"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the meaning Title 1 gives to a time word` `the words calendar year` BECAUSE "Title 1 gives no meaning to the words calendar year"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the meaning Title 1 gives to a time word` `the word session` BECAUSE "Title 1 gives no meaning to the word session"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the meaning Title 1 gives to a time word` `the word forthwith` BECAUSE "Title 1 gives no meaning to the word forthwith"

§ `Part B.1 — section 106, the last six days of a session`

-- Session ends 2026-12-31: the six days are 26, 27, 28, 29, 30 and 31 December.
#ASSERT `the first of the last six days of a session` (YMD 2026 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 12 26
#ASSERT NOT `a date falls in the last six days of a session` (YMD 2026 12 25) (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT     `a date falls in the last six days of a session` (YMD 2026 12 26) (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT     `a date falls in the last six days of a session` (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT `a date falls in the last six days of a session` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31)
-- Session ends 2027-03-03: Mar 3, 2, 1 and Feb 28, 27, 26 (2027 has no 29 February).
#ASSERT `the first of the last six days of a session` (YMD 2027 3 3) EQUALS YMD 2027 2 26
#ASSERT NOT `a date falls in the last six days of a session` (YMD 2027 2 25) (YMD 2027 3 3)
#ASSERT     `a date falls in the last six days of a session` (YMD 2027 2 26) (YMD 2027 3 3)
-- Session ends 2028-03-02: Mar 2, 1 and Feb 29, 28, 27, 26 (2028 is a leap year).
#ASSERT `the first of the last six days of a session` (YMD 2028 3 2) EQUALS YMD 2028 2 26
#ASSERT NOT `a date falls in the last six days of a session` (YMD 2028 2 25) (YMD 2028 3 2)
#ASSERT     `a date falls in the last six days of a session` (YMD 2028 2 29) (YMD 2028 3 2)

§ `Part B.2 — section 204(a) and (b), the day preceding the commencement of the following session`

#ASSERT `the day as at which a Code establishes the law` (YMD 2027 1 3) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 2
#ASSERT `the day as at which a Code establishes the law` (YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 12 31
#ASSERT `the day as at which a Code establishes the law` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `the day as at which a Code establishes the law` (YMD 2028 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2028 2 29

§ `Part B.3 — the words "N days after the date" and "N years after the date" of ss 112b and 202(c)`

#ASSERT `the day that is a number of days after a date` 120 (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 1
#ASSERT `the day that is a number of days after a date` 30 (YMD 2026 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 2
#ASSERT `the day that is a number of days after a date` 15 (YMD 2024 2 20) EQUALS YMD 2024 3 6
#ASSERT `the day that is a number of days after a date` 1 (YMD 2026 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 1
#ASSERT `the day that is a number of years after a date` 3 (YMD 2022 12 23) EQUALS YMD 2025 12 23
#ASSERT `the day that is a number of years after a date` 5 (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 15
#ASSERT `the day that is a number of years after a date` 4 (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2028 2 29
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day that is a number of years after a date` 1 (YMD 2024 2 29) BECAUSE "the same calendar date does not exist that many years after the date, and Title 1 does not say what then"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day that is a number of years after a date` 3 (YMD 2024 2 29) BECAUSE "the same calendar date does not exist that many years after the date, and Title 1 does not say what then"

§ `B.4 — the preceding number of days (section 112b(b)(2))`

-- the posting is on 2026-05-01; the preceding 120 days are 2026-01-01 to 2026-04-30
#ASSERT     `a date falls in the preceding number of days` (YMD 2026 1 1)  (YMD 2026 5 1) 120
#ASSERT     `a date falls in the preceding number of days` (YMD 2026 4 30) (YMD 2026 5 1) 120
#ASSERT NOT `a date falls in the preceding number of days` (YMD 2025 12 31) (YMD 2026 5 1) 120
#ASSERT NOT `a date falls in the preceding number of days` (YMD 2026 5 1)  (YMD 2026 5 1) 120
#ASSERT NOT `a date falls in the preceding number of days` (YMD 2026 5 2)  (YMD 2026 5 1) 120
-- one day: only the day before
#ASSERT     `a date falls in the preceding number of days` (YMD 2026 3 9)  (YMD 2026 3 10) 1
#ASSERT NOT `a date falls in the preceding number of days` (YMD 2026 3 8)  (YMD 2026 3 10) 1
#ASSERT NOT `a date falls in the preceding number of days` (YMD 2026 3 10) (YMD 2026 3 10) 1

§ `B.5 — the period of a number of years beginning on a day (section 112b(h)(1))`

-- nine years beginning on 2020-03-01 end on 2029-02-28
#ASSERT     `a date falls in the period of a number of years beginning on a day` (YMD 2020 3 1)  (YMD 2020 3 1) 9
#ASSERT     `a date falls in the period of a number of years beginning on a day` (YMD 2029 2 28) (YMD 2020 3 1) 9
#ASSERT NOT `a date falls in the period of a number of years beginning on a day` (YMD 2029 3 1)  (YMD 2020 3 1) 9
#ASSERT NOT `a date falls in the period of a number of years beginning on a day` (YMD 2020 2 29) (YMD 2020 3 1) 9
-- a period beginning on 29 February: the ninth anniversary falls in 2033, which has no 29 February
#ASSERT REFUSED `a date falls in the period of a number of years beginning on a day` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2024 2 29) 9 BECAUSE "the same calendar date does not exist that many years after the date, and Title 1 does not say what then"

§ `The brief's worked cases, read in the ordinary sense of "after" (Part B helpers; not rules of Title 1)`

-- Title 1 has no counting rule (Items 1 and 2 above refuse every one of these). These are what the ordinary meaning of "N years after"
-- and "N days after" gives, the same helpers that sections 112b and 202(c) are read through. A month has no helper: Title 1 never says
-- what a month is, and a start on the 31st is the very case the missing rule would decide.
#ASSERT `the day that is a number of years after a date` 3 (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
#ASSERT `the day that is a number of years after a date` 5 (YMD 2025 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 15
#ASSERT `the day that is a number of years after a date` 5 (YMD 2025 9 1)  EQUALS YMD 2030 9 1
#ASSERT `the day that is a number of days after a date` 30 (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `the day that is a number of years after a date` 2 (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day that is a number of years after a date` 1 (YMD 2024 2 29) BECAUSE "the same calendar date does not exist that many years after the date, and Title 1 does not say what then"
